Content:
I think the wagynara probably be good, but I have some critics:
- It is NOT Luciano's carbonara. He uses Grana Padano, and I've watched him doing his carbonara, there is some differences in the tecnique, and in italian cuisine, that make a huge diference;
- Well, the second plate is just TOO expensive for someone normal to replicate, so even it is slightly better in taste, I don't think it is possible for me to spend so much money;
- You are telling to your audience that your replica is the same taste, but I doubt. Please, don't do that.
